h2('7.3 Customer Management');note('Not captured — no separate page exists. Contact fields (name, company, email, phone) live inside the lead record itself; there is no standalone customer entity or screen.')
h2('7.4 Lead Management');note("Not captured as a dedicated screen — the same 'Prioritized leads' table on the Dashboard (Figure 7.2) is the only lead list/CRUD surface; there is no separate Lead Management page.")
h2('7.5 Opportunity Management');note('Not implemented as a separate concept. The system does not distinguish opportunities from leads; a lead record itself represents the deal.')
h2('7.6 Task & Follow-up');note('Not captured — this is backend-only. Follow-up tasks are created and tracked through ReminderWorker, a background service, and are never exposed as a screen.')
h2('7.7 Sales Pipeline');figure(f'{SHOTS}/pipeline.png','Figure 7.7: Sales Pipeline');p('Captured. Drag-and-drop Kanban board; dropping a card issues a status update and broadcasts the change over SignalR.')
h2('7.8 User Management');figure(f'{SHOTS}/admin.png','Figure 7.8: User Management (Admin)');p('Captured. Admin page covering user creation, the audit log, and recovery of deleted leads.')
h2('7.9 Reports & Analytics');note('Not captured as a dedicated page — the only analytics surface is the set of four metric cards on the Dashboard (Figure 7.2); there is no separate Reports & Analytics screen.')
pagebreak()
h1('8 Learning During Project Work');p('The project strengthened our understanding of layered web application development. We learned to separate controllers, business services, data access, and browser presentation so that each responsibility can be tested and changed safely. We practiced Entity Framework Core relationships, fluent configuration, SQL Server foreign keys, and data constraints.');p('We also learned how scoring rules convert sales behavior into a transparent business decision. The activity stream showed the value of consistent timestamps and user references. Building the reminder worker introduced background processing, idempotency through the ReminderSent flag, and error logging. Finally, preparing MIS measures demonstrated how operational data can support management decisions.');
h1('9 Conclusion and Future Scope');p('The Web Based CRM for Small Businesses consolidates lead details, customer interactions, follow-up tasks, automatic priority scoring, and management reporting in one web application. The design reduces dependence on separate spreadsheets and fragmented communication records.');p('Future work can add ASP.NET Core Identity with JWT authentication, email or WhatsApp notification delivery, file attachments, customer portals, configurable scoring weights, advanced charts, exportable reports, and a cloud deployment pipeline.');
